Stores every cost layer (inbound quantity + unit cost) of a product in a specific location, enabling precise perpetual inventory valuation using FIFO, Average, or Standard costing.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Perpetual stock valuation (real-time accounting value)
FIFO costing (oldest layers consumed first)
Average costing (weighted average recalculation)
Cost price updates on receipts, production, and adjustments
Inventory value on Balance Sheet
COGS (Cost of Goods Sold) calculation on delivery/invoice
Stock revaluation and price difference handling
Audit trail of every cost change

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent, high-performance, immutable style)
Key Fields:
product_id → product.product (required)
company_id, location_id → stock.location
quantity (float), remaining_qty (float)
unit_cost (monetary), value (monetary)
stock_move_id → stock.move (source move)
stock_valuation_layer_id (parent layer for adjustments)
description, create_date
Computed: remaining_value

Critical Hooks: create, _svl_reduce, _svl_recompute, action_reset_stock_valuation
Security: stock.group_stock_manager + strict company rules (very protected)

RAG Routing Keywords:
stock valuation layer, valuation layer, svl, stock cost layer, fifo layer, average cost layer, inventory value layer, cost layer, perpetual valuation, stock.valuation.layer, cogs layer, unit cost layer
Related Models (most joined):

product.product (via product_id)
stock.move (via stock_move_id)
stock.quant
account.move.line (via stock valuation → accounting)
stock.location
stock.valuation.layer (parent/child for revaluations)

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
stock.valuation.layer is Odoo’s perpetual costing engine model that records every inbound stock layer with quantity, unit_cost, value, and remaining_qty for a product_id in a location. It powers accurate FIFO/Average costing, real-time inventory valuation, COGS calculation, and automatic generation of accounting entries on stock moves, making it the core of Odoo’s modern Inventory + Accounting integration.